    <sys:String x:Key="LOCQuiverPlayNotSetUp">The game of {0} was not found. Run its "Setup" action to build or install it; if you put it outside the app's folder, choose its program with "Choose game executable..." in the game's menu (Recomps (Quiver Launcher)).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCQuiverChosenExecutable" xml:space="preserve">Playnite will start {0} with:&#x0a;{1}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCQuiverSavesNotYet" xml:space="preserve">{0} has not saved anything yet. Its saves will be in:&#x0a;{1}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCQuiverAchievementsNotYet">{0} has not recorded any achievement yet.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCQuiverAchievementsExported" xml:space="preserve">Experimental: exported {1} achievements of {0} ({2} unlocked) to:&#x0a;{3}&#x0a;&#x0a;To see them in Playnite Achievements, open this game's achievement editor there and import that CSV as its custom achievements. The CSV is rewritten every time the game closes: import it again after unlocking more (rows are matched by ID, nothing is duplicated).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCQuiverAchievementPlaceholder">Achievement {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCQuiverAchievementsNoNames">This game's achievement names are not known yet (they are inside the game's program), so they are exported as "Achievement 1", "Achievement 2"... Importing the CSV again writes those names again over any you typed in Playnite Achievements.</sys:String>
